workflow:
1- user add portal with Add portal
2- user fetches genres of portal
3- user select/enable genres
4- selected genres (and portal) are saved in persistent database (portals tables and genre tables)
5- user closes Add portal
6- channels, vod, series of enabled genres are fetched and saved in persistent database (source tables)
7- user goes to live channels
8- list only shows the saved channels from persistent database (source tables)
9- user enables which channels he wants in output playlist
10- same for vod, series
11- user goes to playlist, lists show only saved channels from persistent database (playlist tables)
12- user gives addition info of enabled channels, like fall back chanbel, custom name, ffmpeg templates, etc.
13- all information is saved in persistent database (playlist tables)
14- same for vod, series
15- if something changes output playlist is updated (only enabled channels for playlist table will be in final output playlist)


proposed Database structure:
Setup a separate docker with a postgres database
required database tables:
** portals **
- portals (1 row per portal)
	portal-ID (unique key)
	portal-name
	portal-URL
	portal-enabled
		portal-org-live-genres
		portal-org-vod-genres
		portal-org-serie-genres
- mac-addresses
	mac-ID (unique key)
	portal-ID (linkkey to portals table)
	mac-address
	mac-password
	mac-expire
	mac-online

** genres **
- live-genres (list with enabled live genres, selected by user)
	live-genres-ID (unique key)
	portal-ID (linkkey to portals table)
	live-genre-name
	live-enabled-genre
		<all additional original information from portal, like channel number, channel name, epg-id, logo, etc.>
- vod-genres (list with enabled vod genres, selected by user)
	vod-genres-ID (unique key)
	portal-ID (linkkey to portals table)
	vod-genre-name
	vod-enabled-genre
		<all additional original information from portal, like channel number, vod name, poster, etc.>
- serie-genres (list with enabled series/providers, selected by user)
	serie-genres-ID (unique key)
	portal-ID (linkkey to portals table)
	serie-genre-name
	serie-enabled-genre
		<all additional original information from portal, like channel number, provider name, serie name, season, logo, etc.>
- local-files
	local-files-ID (unique key)
	local-directory
	local-files

** source **	
- live-source (list of live channels of enabled live genres)
	live-source-ID (unique key)
	live-genres-ID (linkkey to live-genres table)
	live-enabled
	live-original-name
	live-custom-name (original channel name, possible to override with custome channel name)
	live-groupname (original genre name, possible to override with custome group name)
- vod-source (list of vod of enabled vod genres)
	vod-source-ID (unique key)
	vod-genres-ID (linkkey to vod-genres table)
	vod-enabled
	vod-original-name
	vod-custom-name (original vod name, possible to override with custome vod name)
	vod-groupname (original genre name, possible to override with custome group name)
- serie-source (list of series of enabled series/provider genres)
	serie-source-ID (unique key)
	serie-genres-ID (linkkey to serie-genres table)
	serie-enabled
	serie-original-name
	serie-custom-name (original serie name, possible to override with custome serie name)
	serie-groupname (original genre name, possible to override with custome group name)
- local-source (list with local directories)
	local-source-ID (unique key)
	local-directory
	local-enabled

** playlist **
- live-playlist (list of custom channels in final output)
	live-playlist-ID (unique key)
	live-custom-name
	live-groupname (original genre name, possible to override with custome group name)
	live-ffmpeg
	live-logo
	live-fallback-channels (comma separeted list with live-source-ID that fuzy matches the live-original-name)
	live-epg
	live-enabled
	live-order
- vod-playlist (list of vod of enabled vod genres)
	vod-playlist-ID (unique key)
	vod-source-ID (linkkey to vod-source table)
	vod-enabled
	vod-order
	vod-original-name
	vod-groupname (original genre name, possible to override with custome group name)
	vod-custom-name
	vod-ffmpeg
	vod-logo
	vod-fallback-channels (comma separeted list with vod-source-ID that fuzy matches the vod-original-name)
	<all vod information from TMDB>
- serie-playlist (list of series of enabled series/provider genres)
	serie-playlist-ID (unique key)
	serie-source-ID (linkkey to serie-genres table)
	serie-enabled
	serie-order
	serie-original-name
	serie-custom-name
	serie-groupname (original genre name, possible to override with custome group name)
	serie-ffmpeg
	serie-logo
	serie-fallback-channels (comma separeted list with serie-source-ID that fuzy matches the serie-original-name)
	<all serie information from TMDB>
- local-playlist
	local-playlist-ID (unique key)
	local-files-ID (linkkey to local-files table)
	local-name
	local-enabled
	local-order
	local-groupname (default: "vod-local")
	local-ffmpeg

** settings **
- ffmpeg
	ffmpeg-ID (unique key)
	ffmpeg-enabled
	ffmpeg-name
	ffmpeg-resolution
	ffmpeg-ratio
	ffmpeg-video-codex
	ffmpeg-audio-codex
	ffmpeg-bitrate
	<any other missing ffmpeg parameters that needs to be saved>

- users
	user-ID (unique key)
	user-name
	user-password
	user-m3u
	user-xtream
	user-expire
	user-groups (from live-groupname, vod-groupname, serie-groupname, local-groupname)
	
- settings
	setting-ID (unique key)
	<all persistent settings that needs to be stored>


